  {
    "index": 11,
    "hash": "abc1sxOeKBeMhwUqhlfwTGferTk=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-16T20:32:58.720Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## Claim\n\nModel each skill invocation as an attributable transformation: an action against a document, dispatched by an attributed actor, executed by a deterministic reducer, and recorded in an append-only operation log.\n\n## Implications\n\n- State derives only from replaying the log\n- Every byte in the final state traces to an operation \u2192 skill \u2192 actor\n- The artifact and the provenance record are the same structure\n\n## Contrast\n\nTool-call traces that live *beside* the artifact force post-hoc reconciliation. Unifying them (\"the artifact is the log\") removes that gap.\n\n## See also (reweave)\n\n- Related evaluation stance: process-level evaluation beyond output scoring\n- Related memory risk: untyped knowledge-layer contamination modes\n- Implementation conventions: three conventions for attributable skills\n",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-16T20:32:58.720Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-16T20:32:58.720Z"
    }
  },
  {
    "index": 12,
    "hash": "9Pl/RCA3xg0U9HQxXWlq1GqjzQQ=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T10:03:28.032Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## Claim\n\nModel each skill invocation as an attributable transformation: an action against a document, dispatched by an attributed actor, executed by a deterministic reducer, and recorded in an append-only operation log.\n\n## Implications\n\n- State derives only from replaying the log\n- Every byte in the final state traces to an operation \u2192 skill \u2192 actor\n- The artifact and the provenance record are the same structure\n\n## Contrast\n\nTool-call traces that live *beside* the artifact force post-hoc reconciliation. Unifying them (\"the artifact is the log\") removes that gap.\n\n## See also (reweave)\n\n- Related evaluation stance: process-level evaluation beyond output scoring\n- Related memory risk: untyped knowledge-layer contamination modes\n- Implementation conventions: three conventions for attributable skills\n\n\n## Methodology grounding\nThe claims below live in the plugin's `data/methodology/` corpus; the relationship is stated per claim.\n\n- **[[hook enforcement guarantees quality while instruction enforcement merely suggests it]]** \u2014 BUILDS_ON. A skill described in an instruction file is a suggestion; a skill invocation recorded as an operation on document state is enforcement, because the record exists whether or not the agent cooperated.\n- **[[agents are simultaneously methodology executors and subjects creating a unique trust asymmetry]]** \u2014 RELATES_TO. Attribution is the asymmetry's remedy: if every transformation names its actor and its inputs, the agent's dual role stops being invisible to whoever audits the result.\n",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T10:03:28.032Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T10:03:28.032Z"
    }
  }
]